<alcuin. carm. 12.1>	Te deus omnipotens conservet semper ubique,
<alcuin. carm. 12.2>	Iulius o iuvenis, spes amor atque decus.
<alcuin. carm. 12.3>	Lucia vive deo felix, clarissima virgo,
<alcuin. carm. 12.4>	Semper in aeternum, Lucia virgo, vale!
<alcuin. carm. 12.5>	Et mea per versus valeat Mathematica dulces,
<alcuin. carm. 12.6>	Femina verbipotens, tu sine fine vale!
<alcuin. carm. 12.7>	Delia doctisono ... grammatica plectro,
<alcuin. carm. 12.8>	Floreat ut studiis pectus ubique tuum.
<alcuin. carm. 12.9>	Vita, salus cunctis, domino donante, puellis,
<alcuin. carm. 12.10>	Perpetuumque vale in tempora longa fiat.
<alcuin. carm. 12.11>	Felix quippe pater, flores qui germine tales
<alcuin. carm. 12.12>	Egregiis mundi progenuit titulis.
<alcuin. carm. 12.13>	Dextra patris summi natas natosque patremque
<alcuin. carm. 12.14>	Conservet pariter, protegat atque regat.
